# Board 1.62, its second half. A docked terminal gets another font and its window happens to keep its size, so Arbor sees nothing. Asked for
# whole lines of the old font it takes something else, and that ends what was known of its cells: it is offered its slot like a
# window of which nothing is known, and talked down a line if it takes more. It used to be offered the two points over its slot that any
# window is allowed, and allowed two more on top of those: three over, it passed for fitting, then for refusing, and was a tile.
quiet
open Terminal 560x340 cell 7x15
open Notes
open Mail
dock 101 left
dock 103 right
dock 102 right
dock 102 beside 101 bottom

# Until its height has shown its cell.
resize 101 bottom 4
resize 101 bottom 4
resize 101 bottom 4
resize 101 bottom 4
resize 101 bottom 4
resize 101 bottom 4
expect at 101 12 37
expect size 101 700x435

# A smaller font: lines of 11 points. Its slot becomes 448 high; 30 lines of the old font are 450; the nearest lines of the new one 451.
cell 101 5x11
resize 101 bottom 4
expect docked 101
expect at 101 12 37
expect size 101 700x440

# And that is that: the next layouts find nothing to do.
show-all
expect still 101
